  "title": "Under the Hood: Why Our Platform Is Open Source, Modular, and Interoperable",
  "summary": "Every day, corrections software supports decisions with enormous stakes for public safety and people’s liberty. Too often, the agencies responsible for those decisions don't control the technology shaping them. We designed the Recidiviz Corrections Platform differently—an open source software that is modular and interoperable—because software funded with public money should be transparent and agencies should have autonomy and flexibility over their systems.",
